{"meta":{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vTW92aWVzL0JvbGx5d29vZC8yMDExLTIwMTUvR2FsaSUyMEdhbGklMjBDaG9yJTIwSGFpJTIwJTI4MjAxMiUyOS8","type":"movie","name":"Gali Gali Chor Hai","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/3PjM4g5bdl2mkN08E7Ed0WrEzgM.jpg","background":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/nZmziwg43uTaebgtTJCRYSIqnLW.jpg","description":"Bharat is the Indian common man and a part-time actor, and portrays the role of Hanuman, the monkey God, at the local Ramleela skit.  His family consists of his wife, Nisha, ambitious for her husband, and would like him to be promoted from cashier to manager at the bank.  Bharat, however, wants to be Ram, the protagonist in Ramleela.  And then one day, Bharat’s table-fan gets stolen. Bharat then gets sucked into a system that worships corruption and dishonesty, and is forced to bribe his way through criminals and law keepers alike, just to get this table-fan back. What the system does not seem to realise, however, is that even somebody as common as Bharat can snap, and when he does, he can make life hell for a lot of people\n\nReleased 3 Feb 2012 · IN · Language: Hindi\n\nOn your server — Audio: Hindi","releaseInfo":"2012","genres":["Drama","Action","Bollywood"],"imdbRating":"3.9","cast":["Akshaye Khanna","Shriya Saran","Mugdha Godse","Annu Kapoor","Satish Kaushik","Akhilendra Mishra","Vijay Raaz","Veena Malik"],"director":["Rumi Jaffery"],"released":"2012-02-03T00:00:00.000Z","app_extras":{"cast":[{"name":"Rumi Jaffery","character":"Director"},{"name":"Akshaye Khanna","character":"Bharat","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/kRPLQ908NrKejOwG6i3ypBd9qDq.jpg"},{"name":"Shriya Saran","character":"Nisha","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/ioOgKBSCJhOdKoZpg86ld7zANbf.jpg"},{"name":"Mugdha Godse","character":"Amitha","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/7IxEfJkhKujmMBSeQAgkapqmpkW.jpg"},{"name":"Annu Kapoor","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/jeWOeGZYWHAvP3fwSgPyozOyW80.jpg"},{"name":"Satish Kaushik